            {
                "entry_id": "422553fc-94e7-36d8-a968-0004652b3546",
                "word": "anophèle",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "2f4e6358-de7c-4bee-b48e-244eaae3e744",
                        "entry_id": "422553fc-94e7-36d8-a968-0004652b3546",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "anophèles"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "10ce846b-f52f-3090-9977-84396400a45f",
                        "entry_id": "422553fc-94e7-36d8-a968-0004652b3546",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Moustique de la famille des culicidés sous-famille des anophélinés appartenant au genre Anopheles, dont certaines espèces sont responsables de la transmission du paludisme à l'homme."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ea229643-1842-4f04-af0e-dc4506fc57c4",
                                "sense_id": "10ce846b-f52f-3090-9977-84396400a45f",
                                "text": "Notre banale mouche domestique (Musca domestica) se rit du D.D.T. sur presque toute la surface de la Terre, au même titre que certaines espèces d’Anophèles, responsables du paludisme."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6c40faab-6ffe-48fd-a656-a955613c8e39",
                                "sense_id": "10ce846b-f52f-3090-9977-84396400a45f",
                                "text": "On sait que l’immunité antiplasmodium diminue le nombre de gamétocytes viables (c’est-à-dire capables d’évoluer chez l’anophèle)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "44d2d0c3-4223-4f10-bbb6-4faff5d899be",
                                "sense_id": "10ce846b-f52f-3090-9977-84396400a45f",
                                "text": "Et le palu, ça traîne pas comme ça dans l'air. C'est véhiculé par un moustique, l’anophèle."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d9428c9f-83c7-45d1-8c67-d8dc22bc185e",
                                "sense_id": "10ce846b-f52f-3090-9977-84396400a45f",
                                "text": "Vint le beau temps frais, qui emporta les anophèles et ramena un vent printanier."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ea007122-5b93-4ba6-8545-07b424cbcb6c",
                        "source_entry_id": "422553fc-94e7-36d8-a968-0004652b3546",
                        "source_sense_id": "10ce846b-f52f-3090-9977-84396400a45f",
                        "target_lang_word": "anopheles",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "anopheles",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "041a0389-336b-3878-8825-3e47f078aaf3",
                                        "entry_id": "6cf11843-e18b-33b4-8492-585311895d88",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A mosquito of the genus Anopheles, some insects of which transmit various parasites of the genus Plasmodium that are the cause of malaria."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "also",
                                            "attributive",
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3c727e7a-a352-40cc-8a0c-5207c56a955d",
                                                "sense_id": "041a0389-336b-3878-8825-3e47f078aaf3",
                                                "text": "Analogy with the malaria-carrying mosquito points to the various kinds of anopheles, and perhaps to some species of the ordinary mosquito or culex, as being possible bearers of the disease."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f765666-30f9-4d8a-9fc7-571555df3c5e",
                                                "sense_id": "041a0389-336b-3878-8825-3e47f078aaf3",
                                                "text": "[T]he whole business was a silly mistake due to a murderous-mouthed ignorance of the ease with which the same result could have been obtained by inoculation with anopheles vaccine and stegomyia emulsion."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c23782ee-fd4d-43c7-bab0-8db40fc0f6a9",
                                                "sense_id": "041a0389-336b-3878-8825-3e47f078aaf3",
                                                "text": "They slept again, then woke, and drowsed their way slowly towards the late afternoon when the unexpected fever awoke in him—an onslaught so sudden that the symptoms for her seemed instantly recognisable as a rogue attack of malaria. […] \"I brought it back from the desert—they have been planting rice like fools, and now you get anopheles right up to the gates of Alexandria!\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cdbf8034-be2d-4a90-8b38-b3a081ce308b",
                        "source_entry_id": "422553fc-94e7-36d8-a968-0004652b3546",
                        "source_sense_id": "10ce846b-f52f-3090-9977-84396400a45f",
                        "target_lang_word": "anofele",
                        "target_lang_code": "it",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "anofele",
                                "target_lang_code": "it",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "75cce16a-4b99-3c3b-8728-1c3f00ecb063",
